#provision("200.01(1)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(1)")[
  Departure release (DR) is automatically granted once confirmation of the active runway is communicated.
] <p200-01-1>

#provision("200.01(2)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(2)")[
  Should ZXAA\_TWR utilize a non-active runway for departure, they must obtain a DR from the position covering ZXAA\_APP.
] <p200-01-2>

#provision("200.01(3)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(3)")[
  A DR request may be verbally processed or through the use of the ExampleSitu release request function. If the Tower prefers ExampleSitu, inform the departure controller so they can be vigilant of requests.
] <p200-01-3>

#provision("200.01(4)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(4)")[
  Departure release is requested for each aircraft, unless a blanket release applies.
] <p200-01-4>

#provision("200.01(4)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  A blanket release is issued by ZXAA\_APP and remains valid until it is withdrawn.
] <p200-01-4-a>

#provision("200.01(4)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  ZXAA\_APP withdraws a blanket release when traffic or weather no longer permits it.
] <p200-01-4-b>

#provision("200.01(5)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(5)")[
  The following information is exchanged when a DR is requested:
] <p200-01-5>

#provision("200.01(5)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  the aircraft callsign;
] <p200-01-5-a>

#provision("200.01(5)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  the departure runway;
] <p200-01-5-b>

#provision("200.01(5)(c)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(c)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  the intended heading or route; and
] <p200-01-5-c>

#provision("200.01(5)(d)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(d)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  any restrictions that apply to the departure.
] <p200-01-5-d>

#provision("200.02", 3, level-label: "Section", title: [All other ZXEX Airports], level-offset: 2)[

] <p200-02>

#provision("200.02(1)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(1)")[
  All other airports in the Exampleland FIR require prior coordination of a DR.
] <p200-02-1>

#provision("200.02(2)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(2)")[
  The radar position covering terminal or departure services may authorize blanket DR authority depending on their circumstances.
] <p200-02-2>

#provision("200.02(3)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(3)")[
  DR requests are processed as described in #link(<p200-01-3>)[\[200.01(3)\]]\.
] <p200-02-3>

#provision("200.02(4)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(4)")[
  Where a DR is refused, the requesting position holds the aircraft until a new request is made.
] <p200-02-4>

#provision("200.02(4)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The refusing position states the reason for the refusal when it is not obvious.
] <p200-02-4-a>

#provision("200.02(4)(b)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(b)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
  The refusing position says when the next request may be made, if known.
] <p200-02-4-b>

#provision("200.02(5)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(5)")[
  Positions confirm every DR that is exchanged by voice with a readback.
] <p200-02-5>

#provision("200.02(6)", 4, level-label: "Subsection", label: "(6)")[
  Positions tell each other as early as possible when they expect a delay. A delay that is expected to last longer than ten minutes is also passed to the adjacent unit.
] <p200-02-6>

#provision("200.02(6)(a)", 5, level-label: "Paragraph", label: "(a)", italic-label: true, indent: 1)[
